    explore: '- String: start below √(2gR) — it just swings.\n- Between √(2gR) and √(5gR): watch the string go **slack** and the ball fall inside the circle.\n- Above √(5gR): full loops.\n- Switch to a **rod**: it loops above √(4gR) — and is in compression at the top.',
    explain: 'Energy: **v² = v₀² − 2gR(1 − cos φ)** (φ from the bottom). Radially, tension and gravity together supply m v²/R: **T = m(v²/R + g cos φ)**. At the top T = m(v<sub>top</sub>²/R − g), so a string stays taut only if v<sub>top</sub>² ≥ gR, i.e. **v₀ ≥ √(5gR)**. Below that the tension reaches zero above the horizontal — at cos φ = (2gR − v₀²)/(3gR) — and the string goes slack: the ball becomes a projectile until the string snaps taut again. A rod can push, so it only needs v<sub>top</sub> > 0: v₀ > √(4gR).',
    apply: [q('cm7-a', 'A ball on a 1.0 m string must have at least what speed at the bottom to complete the circle?', ['4.4 m/s', '6.3 m/s', '7.0 m/s', '9.8 m/s'], 2, '√(5 × 9.81 × 1) = 7.0 m/s.'), q('cm7-b', 'At the top of the circle, with speed exactly √(gR), the tension is…', ['mg', '2mg', 'zero', '6mg'], 2, 'T = m(v²/R − g) = 0.'), q('cm7-c', 'At the bottom, T exceeds the weight because…', ['the string stretches', 'T − mg must supply mv²/R upwards', 'gravity is stronger there', 'the speed is smallest there'], 1, 'Net inward (upward) force = mv²/R.'), q('cm7-d', 'A rigid rod (instead of a string) lets the ball loop with a smaller speed because…', ['it is lighter', 'it can push as well as pull', 'it reduces gravity', 'it adds energy'], 1, 'Only v_top > 0 is needed.')],
    summary: ['v² = v₀² − 2gR(1 − cos φ); T = m(v²/R + g cos φ).', 'String or inside track: complete only if v₀ ≥ √(5gR) (v_top² ≥ gR).', 'Otherwise T hits zero above the horizontal: slack — then projectile motion.', 'Rod: v₀ > √(4gR); it can be in compression at the top.'],
